  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1113 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nTuesday through Saturday:\n\nLow pressure progressing through northern Ontario and low \npressure developing in the lee of the Colorado Rockies on \nTuesday will allow for broad frontogenesis to develop over the \nUpper Midwest. Expecting the resultant cold front to work its \nway southward through southern Wisconsin Tuesday night into \nWednesday morning (60% chances for thunderstorms, CAPE ~1500 \nJ/kg). 0-6 km bulk shear remains marginal (under 35 kt) through \nWednesday morning, before westerly bulk shear builds to near 50 \nkt Wednesday afternoon. Depending on how long overnight \nconvection lingers, severe may be inhibited Wednesday due to \nlack of instability. However, increasing shear and a front in \nthe region may allow for some severe potential Wednesday and \nWednesday night. Kept PoPs from the NBM due to this uncertainty,\nwith 30-60% chances throughout southern Wisconsin into \nWednesday night. Low pressure ejects into the Ohio Valley \nWednesday night.\n\nAs low pressure weakens and exits to the east on Thursday,\nprecipitation chances exit as well. High pressure briefly builds\nback in Thursday into Friday, but with southern Wisconsin\nremaining on the northern edges of the upper level ridge in a \nmore zonal pattern, may see additional rounds of thunderstorms \nthrough the weekend. As ridging builds across the central Plains,\ntemperatures will also climb back into the mid-80s through the\nweekend.\n\nMH",
